==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Wicked King Hevijak''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''God-Emperor Hevijak''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Hevijak can do a lot for your army, once you gather up enough money for him. For most of the time, he will work as a second [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]], staying in the back and attacking rarely, but with powerful attacks. This makes him fairly versatile and rarely unusable. His higher range for a tank allows him to gain some protection from meatshields and not take the full force of the enemy frontline.

He's nothing special against Reds, as [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]] is a far better specialist tanker, while [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Dread Pirate Catley]] already exists for knocking them back, not to mention other, more effective attackers. Red enemies are often way too aggressive and must be subdued with an equal amount of brute force or crowd-controlling effects, with knockback being a subpar option and tanking only feasible for units with lower recharge times.

Hevijak has better matchups against Aku, as he can pierce their [[Shield]]s and his resistance allows him to tank Aku's [[Surge Attack|Surges]] for his other abilities to come into play. There's also the general lack of alternatives. His range isn't the highest, but it's enough to stay clear of [[Fallen Bear]] and [[Dark Priest Mamon]]. Additionally, Hevijak can make it inside [[Ackey]]'s blindspot, though this depends on your meatshields and the enemies supporting Ackey. Since his supporters will be less likely to hold the ground as well, he'll have to rely on his health more, meaning that he can still turn into a waste of money if summoned without the proper support. With the proper support and skill, Hevijak can be a staple on many [[:Category:Anti-Aku Cats|anti-Aku]] lineups.

Needless to say, Hevijak doesn't perform well outside of his niche, so it isn't recommended to use him on mixed stages (unless, of course, if you can utilize his raw damage).

==='''True Form'''===
Hevijak's main gain in this form is his guaranteed chance to knockback his targets, making it that much easier to regain ground. Even when against Shielded Aku enemies, the only thing he needs is a well-placed Shield Pierce or assistance from other units. This turns Hevijak into an incredibly aggressive tank, pushing Aku and Red enemies back with ease. This can help in a pinch, giving space for repositioning and saving up money. The other stat increases are good to have, but being a speciality unit that works defensively, the health and range boosts (can only outrange [[Lord of Ruin Jagando]] by 5) are more important, whereas the damage boost, while not bad at all, doesn't do much, even if it makes his presence much more impactful. Considering it requires rare and elusive materials, this may not be the True Form for everyone, but some will always find it necessary if they lack alternatives or if they're used to having Hevijak around for Aku anyways.

Apart from that, Hevijak also gains a [[Cat Combo]] with [[Ancient Egg: N103 (Rare Cat)|Gas Mask Cat]] and [[Killer Cat (Rare Cat)|Radical Cat]], boosting unit health by 20% for only three slots. Considering all three units do enjoy a good health increase with their roles and due to its sheer efficiency, getting this True Form even if just for the Combo might be actually worth it.

==='''Talents'''===
Knockback Immunity is good for its cost, albeit not needed, as he can now theoretically hold the frontline for a long period of time and absorb damage without having to worry about being pushed back to the base. In practice, this is mainly used to counter annoying Red Enemies with Knockback, like [[Masked Okame]] and [[Red EnerG]]. Other than this, Knockback has little practical application, unless using Hevijak in mixed stages with enemies that abuse said abilities such as [[Trolly Blogger]]s. Wave Immunity is mainly there to prevent him from getting chipped to before he reaches the frontline or to avoid waves that carry debuffs, like waves from [[Infernal Pegasus Deonil]], [[Possessed Empress]] and [[Wicked Face]]. It can also expand his general usage to wave-heavy stages like [[Rickety Coaster]], making him useful for crowned [[Stories of Legend]]. Strengthen is irrelevant, since Hevijak is a defense-oriented unit, but it can be useful for pushing back when trapped against the base or to throw in some last damage before dying.

